{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (cobbler orchestrator) has assigned stitch task #5506 to implement srd078-sum requirements R2.1, R2.2, R3.1, and R3.2 for cmd/sum. Specifically:\n   - R2.1: Add `-r` flag to select BSD checksum algorithm (which is already the default behavior)\n   - R2.2: Add `-s` flag to select System V checksum algorithm (16-bit sum of all bytes, 512-byte block size)\n   - R3.1: Exit 0 when all files processed successfully (already implemented in existing code)\n   - R3.2: Exit 1 when any file cannot be opened (already implemented in existing code)\n   \n   Acceptance criteria: go build, go vet, and go test must all pass for ./cmd/sum/.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - BSD checksum: 16-bit rotating checksum, 1024-byte block size (already implemented)\n   - System V checksum: 16-bit sum of all bytes, 512-byte block size (needs implementation)\n   - Differential testing against `gsum` (Homebrew GNU coreutils reference binary)\n   - SIGPIPE handler via pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n   - Flag parsing for `-r` and `-s` flags\n   - Output format: \"CHECKSUM BLOCKS FILENAME\" for both algorithms\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max (E8)\n   - No git commands allowed (orchestrator manages git)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd078-sum.yaml**\n     - Source of truth for requirements R2.1, R2.2, R3.1, R3.2\n     - R2.1: `-r` selects BSD (default), 16-bit rotating checksum, 1024-byte blocks\n     - R2.2: `-s` selects System V, 16-bit sum of all bytes, 512-byte blocks\n     - R3.1: Exit 0 on success; R3.2: Exit 1 on file open failure\n\n   - **cmd/sum/main.go** (existing, 67 lines)\n     - Needs modification to add flag parsing and System V algorithm\n     - Current code has BSD-only implementation with no flag parsing\n     ```go\n     package main\n     \n     import (\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"io\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     \n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         files := os.Args[1:]\n         exitCode := 0\n         if len(files) == 0 {\n             checksum, totalBytes, err := bsdChecksum(os.Stdin)\n             if err != nil {\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"sum: stdin: %v\\n\", err)\n                 os.Exit(1)\n             }\n             blocks := (totalBytes + 1023) / 1024\n             fmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"%05d %5d\\n\", checksum, blocks)\n         } else {\n             for _, file := range files {\n                 f, err := os.Open(file)\n                 if err != nil {\n                     fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"sum: %v\\n\", err)\n                     exitCode = 1\n                     continue\n                 }\n                 checksum, totalBytes, err := bsdChecksum(f)\n                 f.Close()\n                 if err != nil {\n                     fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"sum: %v\\n\", err)\n                     exitCode = 1\n                     continue\n                 }\n                 blocks := (totalBytes + 1023) / 1024\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stdout, \"%05d %5d %s\\n\", checksum, blocks, file)\n             }\n         }\n         os.Exit(exitCode)\n     }\n     \n     func bsdChecksum(r io.Reader) (uint16, int64, error) {\n         var checksum uint16\n         var totalBytes int64\n         buf := make([]byte, 32*1024)\n         for {\n             n, err := r.Read(buf)\n             for _, b := range buf[:n] {\n                 checksum = (checksum >> 1) + ((checksum & 1) << 15)\n                 checksum += uint16(b)\n             }\n             totalBytes += int64(n)\n             if err == io.EOF {\n                 break\n             }\n             if err != nil {\n                 return 0, 0, err\n             }\n         }\n         return checksum, totalBytes, nil\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **cmd/sum/sum_test.go** (existing, 134 lines)\n     - Needs modification to add test cases for -r and -s flags\n     - Currently has fixture files: hello.txt, empty.txt, binary.dat, large.txt\n     - Tests R1.1-R1.4 with differential testing against gsum\n     - Has TestSIGPIPE test\n     - Uses discardStderr normalizer for error tests\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet; implementation has not started.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that R3.1 (exit 0 on success) and R3.2 (exit 1 on failure) are already implemented in the existing code through the `exitCode` variable and `os.Exit(exitCode)` pattern.\n   - The main new work is: (a) adding flag parsing for -r and -s, (b) implementing the System V checksum algorithm, (c) using the correct block size per algorithm, and (d) adding differential test cases.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The initial massive task prompt from the cobbler orchestrator with full project context, task specification, constraints, SRD, architecture, and execution constitution.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Modify cmd/sum/main.go: Add flag parsing for -r/-s, implement System V checksum algorithm (sysVChecksum function), adjust block size calculation based on algorithm (1024 for BSD, 512 for System V)\n   - Modify cmd/sum/sum_test.go: Add differential test cases for `-r` flag and `-s` flag\n   - Run `go build -o bin/sum ./cmd/sum/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/sum/` to check for issues\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/sum/ -count=1` to verify all tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all three required files (SRD, main.go, sum_test.go) and was about to begin implementation. I had analyzed:\n   - The existing code structure and what's already implemented\n   - What specifically needs to change: flag parsing (os.Args manual parsing since this project do